A delay forgets the tick the call landed in:
a delay of zero arms a timer line for the tick already counted, and every deadline comes a tick early.
The tick fires every due timer line,
so an Irq armed on one has its deadline ahead of the count.
The demo times its sleeps on the clock, which now keeps pace with the tick, and finds them short.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ static uint32_t delay_ticks(uint32_t us)
  */
 static uint32_t delay_deadline(uint32_t ticks)
 {
-    return sched_ticks + ticks + 1;
+    return sched_ticks + ticks;
 }
 
